 All product endpoints are JSON endpoints under `/api/v1`. Requests other than account creation select a business with `X-Helpdesk-Account`. Authenticated requests use `Authorization: Bearer TOKEN`.
 
-Customers register at `POST /api/v1/registrations`, then use the standard verification and session endpoints. Authenticated customers use `/api/v1/requests` and its nested `/comments` route; staff use `/api/v1/tickets`. Replies and status changes are submitted with `PATCH`. Lists accept `page` and `per_page` and include pagination metadata with the records.
+Customers register at `POST /api/v1/registrations`, then use the standard verification and session endpoints. Authenticated customers use `/api/v1/requests` and its nested `/comments` route; staff use `/api/v1/tickets`. Replies, status changes, and active-staff assignments are submitted with `PATCH`. Private staff comments are excluded from customer comment responses and do not touch the customer request timestamp. Lists accept `page` and `per_page` and include pagination metadata with the records.
+
+Admins manage staff invitations through `/api/v1/invitations`, including list/show, `POST /api/v1/invitations/:id/resend`, and `DELETE /api/v1/invitations/:id`. Invitations expire after seven days. The frontend previews a token with `POST /invitation_previews` (also available at `/api/v1/invitation_previews`) and accepts it at `POST /api/v1/invitation_acceptances`. Accepted staff are verified immediately.
+
+Admins list and inspect users at `/api/v1/users` and update roles or suspension at `/api/v1/users/:id`. User lists can filter by `role` and `suspended`. `GET /api/v1/staff` returns all active admin and agent choices for ticket assignment. Suspending a user revokes their sessions and clears their ticket assignments; the last active admin cannot be suspended or demoted.
 
 Verification and password-reset emails contain links to the configured frontend URL. The confirmation API endpoints are `/api/v1/email_verifications/confirm` and `/api/v1/password_resets/confirm`.
 
